# W44-phase3-B7c — Butteraugli TLS pool vs Mutex pool — HONEST-STOP

## Status

[RULED OUT — measurement shipped, source change reverted on butteraugli/main]

B6 audit ranked B7c as Tier-3 (MED risk, ~2d wall). Implementation went per
spec; measurement showed +3.6 % wall regression on every cell. Reverted.

## Methodology

Paired interleaved A/B, two separate binaries linked against:
- **PRE_B7C**: butteraugli `dd12b90f` (the B7a+b parent — Mutex<Vec<Vec<f32>>>)
- **POST_B7C**: butteraugli `59aeb1a7` (the B7c TLS pool — reverted on main)

Both binaries use the same `jxl-encoder` example
`w44_phase3_b7c_tls_pool_ab.rs`. Encoder code is identical between the
two; only the linked butteraugli changes.

Per-binary: 4 cells × 6 timed encode iters at distance=1.0, effort=9,
default 8-thread rayon pool, on Zen 4 7950X (water-cooled, no thermal
throttling).

Order: 3 outer ROUNDS alternating launch order (odd rounds PRE first,
even rounds POST first) to remove run-order bias. Per cell, the
median of 6 iters is reported; per round, the median of medians
across PRE / POST is paired.

