## Acceptance gates

| gate | target | result |
|---   |---     |---     |
| (a) Build PASS (default + `gpu-butteraugli`) | clean | PASS (default-features only verified; cubecl deps not available locally) |
| (b) Lib tests | butteraugli 87+ / jxl-encoder 1477+ | PASS (87 + 1477) |
| (c) Hash-locks 36/36 + libjxl 4/4 BYTE-IDENTICAL | mandatory | PASS — zero regen needed (pool internals are quantization-neutral) |
| (d) Drift 7/7 PASS | mandatory | PASS |
| (e) Multi-decoder roundtrip on 2 cells × 2 decoders | 4/4 | N/A (no encoder change — only butteraugli internal alloc behaviour) |
| (f) **Wall-time improvement ≥ 1 % on 8-thread runs** | **median improved ≥ 1 %** | **FAIL — +3.6 % REGRESSION** |
| (g) Single-thread wall ±0.5 % | parity | not measured (gate f already failed at 8 thread) |

## Per-cell results (3-round paired A/B)

| cell           | pre_median_ms | post_median_ms | delta_pct | per-round_pct                |
|---             |---            |---             |---        |---                           |
| 02809272b4ca   | 1101.02       | 1142.70        | **+3.79** | +3.79 / +7.01 / +1.39        |
| 097cb426910b   |  769.81       |  813.77        | **+5.71** | +5.71 / +9.04 / +1.68        |
| 0c49a5cce349   |  944.20       |  985.98        | **+4.42** | +4.42 / +8.66 / -3.04        |
| 11f2b039b293   |  868.51       |  872.94        | **+0.51** | +0.51 / +5.67 / -2.90        |

- Overall **median wall delta: +4.11 %** REGRESSION
- Mean: +3.61 %
- 0 / 4 cells improved
- 3 / 4 cells regressed by ≥ 1 %

## Root cause

The TLS architecture INCREASED fresh allocations by segregating buffers
per worker thread, undoing B7a+b's alloc-count reduction:

- **Shared Mutex pool (pre-B7c)**: 48 globally-shared slots converge to
  the steady-state working set. Thread A puts a 1 MB buffer → thread B
  can reuse it on the next iter.
- **TLS pool (B7c)**: cap 16 / thread × 8 threads = up to 128 slots
  THEORETICALLY, but per-thread isolation means buffers stay pinned to
  whichever thread first put them. Thread B that needs a 1 MB buffer
  thread A holds has to either fall through to the shared overflow OR
  fresh-allocate. The overflow path is rare because thread A's TLS
  caps at 16 (so its puts succeed there).

The B6 audit had pegged Mutex contention as the predicted bottleneck.
Back-of-envelope: ~408 pool ops / encode × ~50 ns / op = ~20 µs of
Mutex time out of ~900 ms wall = **0.002 %**. The Mutex was never
the bottleneck. The TLS lookup overhead (`ThreadLocal::get_or` atomic
load + `RefCell::borrow_mut` runtime check + best-fit scan) plus the
EXTRA fresh allocations from per-thread segregation outweighed any
contention savings.

## Why this matters for B7d

B7c is a STRONG signal that pool synchronisation is not the
wall-time bottleneck in CPU butteraugli. The remaining win lives in
the data-movement layer:

- Multi-pass pipeline reads/writes 12 MB of XYB to DRAM, then re-reads
  it 3× for LF/MF/HF blurs (B6 audit, "Cache behaviour" section).
- Half-res pipeline parallels with full-res via `rayon::join`,
  doubling the resident working set during the overlap window.

B7d (strip-tile the entire UHF→MF→LF chain so intermediates stay
L2-resident) is the only remaining B6 candidate that addresses the
real bottleneck. B6 estimated 30-50 % wall reduction at 1024²+,
HIGH risk, 5-7 d.

## DO NOT respawn B7c

- The +3.6 % regression is not a tuning artifact: ALL 4 cells regressed
  in round 1 (when the binary was freshly warm). Variance across rounds
  (cell #4 ranging -2.9 % to +5.7 %) is run-to-run noise; the central
  tendency (+4.1 % median, +3.6 % mean) is clearly negative.
- A different TLS cap (8 instead of 16) would just shift the
  segregation / overflow balance. The structural problem is that
  per-thread isolation is the WRONG architecture when the alloc-count
  reduction is what matters — and B7a+b already achieved that with the
  Mutex pool.
- The `iir-blur` pre-existing non-determinism bug (B7a+b memo) is
  still open; B7c neither caused nor fixed it.

## Reproduction

```bash
BUTTERAUGLI_PRE_REF=dd12b90f \
BUTTERAUGLI_POST_REF=59aeb1a7 \
./scripts/run_w44_phase3_b7c_ab.sh
```

The bench example `w44_phase3_b7c_tls_pool_ab.rs` is retained in
`jxl-encoder/examples/` because it works as a generic wall-time probe
for B7d / future pool-design measurement work — pass `B7C_LABEL=…` to
tag the output.

## Files

- `benchmarks/w44_phase3_b7c_tls_pool_ab_2026-05-23.tsv` — paired
